  "result": "All existing tests pass with the fix.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in `src/generators/utils/parse.ts:146`. The delimiter regex `/\\s*={2,}\\s*/gm` used to split theme-fix records was matching *any* run of 2+ `=` characters anywhere in the text \u2014 including the `==` padding at the end of base64-encoded data URLs embedded in custom CSS. This caused the parser to incorrectly split records mid-line, leaking trailing CSS fragments (like `') !important;`) into `domainPatterns`, which later crashed `createUrlRegex` with an \"Unmatched )\" error.\n\nFix: anchor the delimiter regex to whole lines (`^\\s*={2,}\\s*$`) so it only matches lines that consist solely of `=` characters (optionally surrounded by whitespace), not incidental `==` sequences within CSS/base64 content.\n\nRan the relevant narrow test suites (`tests/config` and `tests/generators/utils`) \u2014 all 13 tests pass.",
